dsv41 patch 0058 (20.10.2026): vLLM's OffloadingConnector next to PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True.
Why: vllm/config/vllm.py _verify_kv_transfer_compat rejects every KV connector when the PyTorch allocator uses
expandable segments (CUDA VMM can remap a virtual range to other physical pages, which breaks connectors that register
GPU memory for RDMA once). We run with expandable segments (about 1 GiB more free memory per node in our runs). The
OffloadingConnector (vLLM's own CPU + file-system KV tier) copies blocks between the GPU cache and
pinned host buffers by virtual address at copy time, registers only host memory (cudaHostRegister), and the KV cache is
one allocation held for the engine's lifetime, so the hazard does not apply to it. Without the patch the engine exits
17 s into the start ("expandable_segments" ValueError).
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_OFFLOAD_EXPANDABLE_OK=1 (default 0 = check as before), only for kv_connector "OffloadingConnector".
Not measured live yet: the offload window (cold 60K prompt -> restart -> reload from SSD -> corrupted block -> CRC miss,
patch 0056) is still to run.

--- a/vllm/config/vllm.py
+++ b/vllm/config/vllm.py
@@ -1223,6 +1223,15 @@
             or self.kv_transfer_config.kv_connector is None
         ):
             return
+        # dsv41 patch 0058 (VLLM_DSV41_OFFLOAD_EXPANDABLE_OK=1, default off): the OffloadingConnector copies KV
+        # blocks between the GPU cache and pinned host buffers by virtual address at copy time and registers no GPU
+        # memory, and the KV cache is one allocation held for the engine's lifetime (never freed, so never remapped).
+        # The stale-registration hazard below does not apply to it.
+        if (
+            os.environ.get("VLLM_DSV41_OFFLOAD_EXPANDABLE_OK", "0") == "1"
+            and self.kv_transfer_config.kv_connector == "OffloadingConnector"
+        ):
+            return
 
